# Demo cases

A case is `configs/<id>.yaml` (+ optional `knowledge/<id>_experience.md`). Agent/crew/flow code stays generic.

Required YAML fields (see `CaseConfig` in `config.py` and `configs/titanic.yaml`): `case_id`, `kaggle_competition`, `problem_statement`, `problem_type`, `target_column`, `id_column`, `evaluation_metric`, `data.{train_csv,test_csv,sample_submission_csv}`, `feature_hints`, `success_criterion`.

`--case X` loads `configs/X.yaml`. `maads data download --case X` needs `CASE_SHORTHANDS` in `data_utils.py`. Arbitrary Kaggle slugs use `--competition`.

```yaml
# ✅ GOOD — case-specific knowledge in YAML
feature_hints:
  categorical: [Pclass, Sex, Embarked]
success_criterion:
  metric: accuracy
  threshold: 0.77

# ❌ BAD — in agents.py / capabilities
if case_id == "titanic":
    encode_sex()
```
